                <pb facs="0584" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5445: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-05T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1928—8
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>61. Your 108, March 5, 10 a.m. Zepeda states he will immediately telegraph
                    Chamorro recommending that electoral law be passed at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
